# vdbposmap

- Label: VDB Position Map
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbposmap.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a Vector VDB in which each voxel holds its own position. It works on the topology of the input VDB, so the output matches that structure. Output: pos.
- Résumé (FR) : Produit un VDB vectoriel où chaque voxel stocke sa position, exprimée en espace monde, image, texture ou voxel.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: Float or Vector VDB whose topology is used to compute voxel locations"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the VDB type the source accepts", "Space: World (where the voxel appears in the viewport); Image (unrotated, untranslated location, voxel index scaled by voxel size); Texture (position relative to the VDB's current bounding box); Voxel (voxel index)"]

- Caveats: ["Texture space is relative to the VDB's current bounding box; because VDBs often change size, these values are not very stable"]

